
Basic Installation
==================

How to install this software:

  1. If you start from the dir where this file is...

  3. Type './configure'

  2. Type 'make' 

  3. Type 'make install' (as root)

  4. Type './upgrade' (as user)
     If you've got a preveous version of Jags installed 
     you should run upgrade.

  5. Type 'jags' to run the program. Now config-files will 
     be copied to your home-dir. You now need to open the 
     preferences dialog and set the preferences your way. 
     
Note: When you've updated the preferences please collapse 
      the root-tree before you do anything else.

Note: If're you're upgrading your plugins won't update 
      automaticly. Please run the upgrade-script found 
      in the same directory as this file.

Requirements
============

+ Gtk+ 1.2.* development-package (http://www.gtk.org)

+ Sh-compatible shell, grep, cut, awk and other unix tools

+ Samba-client and nmblookup, included in the samba 
  distribution (http://www.samba.org) and maybe smbmount.

+ A filebrowser, for example gmc or kfm or maybe xterm...

You also need to know one workgroup on your network.

